{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Feynman&limit=10&title=The Meaning of It All","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"titleInfo":{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"The  "},"title":"meaning of it all","subTitle":"thoughts of a citizen scientist"},"name":{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Feynman, Richard Phillips.","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Trivia and miscellanea"},"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"mau"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"Massachusetts"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Reading, Mass"}}],"publisher":"Addison Wesley","dateIssued":["c1998",{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"1998"}],"issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"133 p. ; 22 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Review","#text":"\"In April 1963, Richard P. Feynman gave a series of remarkable lectures at the University of Washington in Seattle. These three consecutive talks were classic Feynman - full of wit and wisdom - but their subject matter was wholly unexpected: Feynman spoke not as a physicist but as a concerned fellow citizen, revealing his uncommon insights into the religious, political, and social issues of the day.\" \"Now, at last, these lectures have been published under the collective title The Meaning of It All. Here is Feynman on mind reading and the laws of probability and statistics; on Christian Science and the dubious effect of prayer on healing; and on human interpersonal relationships. Here is the citizen-scientist on the dramatic effect simple engineering projects could have on the plague of poverty; the vital role creativity plays in science; the conflict between science and religion; the efficacy of doubt and uncertainty in arriving at scientific truths; and why honest politicians can never be successful.\"--Jacket."},"tableOfContents":"The uncertainty of science -- The uncertainty of values -- This unscientific age.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Richard P. Feynman."},"Includes index."],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Science","Social aspects"],"genre":"Miscellanea"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Religion and science"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Religion and Science"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"Q175.5 .F52 1998"},{"@authority":"nlm","#text":"500 F435m"},{"@edition":"21","@authority":"ddc","#text":"500"}],"relatedItem":[{"titleInfo":{"title":"Helix books"}},{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":{"title":"Meaning of it all"},"name":{"namePart":"Feynman, Richard Phillips."},"originInfo":{"publisher":"Reading, Mass. : Addison-Wesley, ©1998"},"identifier":{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)605541832"}},{"@type":"series","titleInfo":{"title":"Helix book"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990077299680203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0201360802"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^^97048250^//r98"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"38039679"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000463633307","#text":"Lamont Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"Q175.5 .F52 1998"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/000000046073724X","#text":"Cabot Science Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"Q175.5 .F52 1998"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener